<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Unholy Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Best in Slot Gear for Unholy Death Knight DPS Phase 2</span></h2>With the release of both 10m and 25m comes a glut of new items and choices, the vast majority stronger than our Phase 1 gear. With split lockouts the sheer amount of gear you can see every week has increased, and so has the ease of gearing. When looking at item levels, it's important to remember that Hard Mode gear uses item levels a tier higher than its difficulty. With that in mind, we're still typically seeking just for the highest density of stats, with a focus on strength items over nearly any other alternative.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - is still the absolute best stat for Unholy Death Knights, this will not change throughout the expansion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - to at least 8% Melee Hit  so your ghoul, gargoyle, and army of the dead as well as main hand specials will be capped, any point of hit after this will increase your spell hit and white auto attack hit chance. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50138/nerves-of-cold-steel">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nerves of Cold Steel</span></a> does not affect your summon or spell hit, but does work for your own melee attacks and specials.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - because we value increasing our gargoyles attack speed so much, on top of the base attack speed gain of haste, this stat is incredibly attractive to us.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit - is a great stat because of how it empowers our AoE, as even though Diseases can't crit, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49655/wandering-plague">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_callofbone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wandering Plague</span></a> is based off of our crit rating.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise has less of a gain for Death Knight's compared to most classes, as our special abilities don't charge us runes if they're dodged, but that strike will still be delayed the lost GCD, and your white hits can be dodged.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;"></div>
<br/>
<br/>This set will put us over the 'soft' cap for hit rating of 8%, but as a dual wield class that's ok, as we still value hit rating highly for our auto attacks.<br/>
<br/>
